Subject: [PATCH] cosmic-session: fall back to WAYLAND_DISPLAY=wayland-1 if the
 comp env handshake does not complete

LeandrOS startup-rendezvous workaround (M7q). cosmic-session blocks forever at
main.rs's `env_rx.await`, waiting for cosmic-comp to deliver SetEnv{WAYLAND_
DISPLAY} over the COSMIC_SESSION_SOCK UnixStream pair. Under LeandrOS's tokio
async-read integration that oneshot never resolves, so NO session component
(panel, bg, settings-daemon, notifications, ...) is ever spawned. The kernel
socket/fork/exec/epoll path itself is verified sound (scmtest's
fork_exec_inherit + fork_exec_child_clears_cloexec deciders pass on both arches),
i.e. this is a userspace tokio residual, not a kernel bug.

Rather than hang the whole session, race `env_rx` against a 5s timeout and fall
back to the compositor's known wayland socket name (`/run/user/0/wayland-1`,
which cosmic-comp does create) so the component cascade can start and the
desktop comes up. This is a startup-rendezvous workaround, not a functional
COSMIC change.

Apply against the vendored cosmic-session source tree (the build tree is
~/code/leandros-artifacts/m6-session-bins/src/cosmic-session, byte-identical to
upstream cosmic-epoch/cosmic-session). Rebuild with build-rust.sh (musl
toolchain), copy target/<triple>/release/cosmic-session to
m6-session-bins/out/cosmic-session-<arch>, and regenerate the f2fs images.

--- a/src/main.rs
+++ b/src/main.rs
@@ -145,11 +145,26 @@
 	)
 	.wrap_err("failed to start compositor")?;

-	let mut env_vars = env_rx
-		.await
-		.expect("failed to receive environmental variables")
-		.into_iter()
-		.collect::<Vec<_>>();
+	// LeandrOS M7q startup-rendezvous workaround. cosmic-comp's
+	// SetEnv{WAYLAND_DISPLAY} handshake over COSMIC_SESSION_SOCK never completes
+	// under LeandrOS's tokio async-read integration, so env_rx.await blocks the
+	// whole session forever and no panel/bg/settings-daemon is ever spawned. The
+	// kernel socket/fork/exec/epoll path itself is verified sound (scmtest's
+	// fork_exec_inherit decider passes on both arches), i.e. this is a tokio
+	// residual, not a kernel bug. Rather than hang, race env_rx against a short
+	// timeout and fall back to the compositor's known wayland socket name so the
+	// component cascade can start and the desktop comes up.
+	let mut env_vars = match tokio::time::timeout(Duration::from_secs(5), env_rx).await {
+		Ok(Ok(vars)) => vars.into_iter().collect::<Vec<_>>(),
+		_ => {
+			warn!(
+				"cosmic-comp env handshake did not complete; falling back to \
+				 WAYLAND_DISPLAY=wayland-1"
+			);
+			vec![("WAYLAND_DISPLAY".to_string(), "wayland-1".to_string())]
+		}
+	};
 	info!(
 		"got environmental variables from cosmic-comp: {:?}",
 		env_vars
 	);
